var users = new List<User>
{
    new User { Id = 1, Name = "Anna", Age = 20, City = "Moscow" },
    new User { Id = 2, Name = "Boris", Age = 35, City = "Saint-Petersburg" },
    new User { Id = 3, Name = "Victor", Age = 20, City = "Moscow" },
    new User { Id = 4, Name = "Darya", Age = 42, City = "Kazan" }
};

. Filtration (to filter collection) Example (Where):

var moscowUsers = users.Where(u => u.City == "Moscow")

output: Anna(20), Victor(20)

. Projection (to transform collection to other view, for example we need only one property or we need to create new object) Example (Select):

var users = users.Select(u => u.Name);

output: Anna, Boris, Darya, Victor

. Sorting (to order collection) Example (OrderBy, ThenBy):

var sortedUsers = users.OrderBy(u => u.Age).ThenBy(u => u.Name);

output: Anna(20), Victor(20), Boris(35), Darya(42)

. Aggregation (when a single summary number or value needs to be calculated from an entire collection) Example (Average, Count, Sum):

double averageAge = users.Average(u => u.Age);

output = 29.25

. Grouping (to organise elements of a collectionn into groups based on shared key) Example (GroupBy):

var groupedByCity = users.GroupBy(u => u.City);

foreach (var group in groupedByCity)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"City: {group.Key}");
    foreach (var user in group)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($" - {user.Name}");
    }
}

output:

City: Moscow
- Anna
- Victor
City: Saint-Petersburg
- Boris
City: Kazan
- Darya
